From 7341307e425fb8c0f7f6a1aaabe208675c8ffc14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab-admin <homelab-admin@homelab>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:20:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] db: add Spotify-account identity columns and
 persistence

The login identity and the Spotify account are being decoupled, so the row
needs somewhere to record whose listening the stored cookies actually read.
Adds nullable users.spotify_account_email and users.spotify_account_name,
plus setSpotifyIdentity/getSpotifyIdentity on the repository.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS cannot add a column to an existing table, so every
installed database needs an explicit ALTER. _ensureLateUsersColumns runs on
each connection, guarded by PRAGMA table_info: a fresh database is born with
the columns, an upgraded one gains them once, and a restart or second worker
thread is a no-op. ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN with no default is metadata-only in
SQLite, so it is safe against a populated table.
